      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "The calorific value of fuel is the amount of heat produced by the complete combustion of 1 kg of fuel. Now, Heat produced by 4.5 kg of fuel = 180000 kJ. Therefore, heat produced by 1 kg of fuel = \\frac{180000}{4.5} = 40000 kJ/kg. Hence, the calorific value of the fuel is 40,000 kJ/kg.",
    "answer_latex": "CV = \\frac{180000}{4.5} = 40000 \\text{ kJ/kg}",
